I think this is not a bug and is finally working as intended=E2=80=A6 but I=
 could be wrong.

FYI some information is here as well:
https://github.com/intel/tpm2-tools/issues/680

For RSA:
I don=E2=80=99t think it=E2=80=99s a bug. You can=E2=80=99t encrypt data la=
rger than the keysize and sometimes
smaller based on padding scheme. I don=E2=80=99t see a way to do a sequence=
 with RSA
algorithms.

I think the code before in the tools was glossing over this bug and you are=
 not getting what you
expect.

On 1.1.1 the input file was read with: loadDataFromFile. Both tools re usin=
g this routine.

The code below, looks like it would just read size bytes. Size has remained
constant through all revisions as the message size of a TPM2B_PUBLIC_KEY_RSA
type for the RSA tool. It looks like size has also remained constant in the=
 tpm2_create
tool.

int loadDataFromFile(const char *fileName, UINT8 *buf, UINT16 *size)
{
    UINT16 count =3D 1, left;
    FILE *f;
    if ( size =3D=3D NULL || buf =3D=3D NULL || fileName =3D=3D NULL )
        return -1;

    f =3D fopen(fileName, "rb+");
    if( f =3D=3D NULL )
    {
        printf("File(%s) open error.\n", fileName);
        return -2;
    }

    left =3D *size;
    *size =3D 0;
    while( left > 0 && count > 0 )
    {
        count =3D fread(buf, 1, left, f);
        *size +=3D count;
        left -=3D count;
        buf +=3D count;
    }

    if( *size =3D=3D 0 )
    {
        printf("File read error\n");
        fclose(f);
        return -3;
    }
    fclose(f);
    return 0;
}



